# DV-006 Navigation

**Document Type:** Development Documentation
**Project:** WissensWerk Template
**Status:** Draft
**Version:** 1.0
**Last Updated:** 28.07.2026

---

# 1. Purpose

This document describes the technical implementation of the website navigation within the WissensWerk Joomla template.

The objective is to provide a navigation system that is:

* responsive
* accessible (WCAG compliant)
* maintainable
* fully compatible with Joomla 5
* based on Bootstrap 5
* visually independent through custom SCSS

The navigation shall integrate seamlessly into the overall template architecture while remaining fully update-safe.

---

# 2. Objectives

The navigation should provide:

* Clear and intuitive user guidance
* Responsive behavior across all device sizes
* Keyboard accessibility
* Support for screen readers
* Clean separation of structure, design and behavior
* Maximum compatibility with Joomla's menu system

---

# 3. Design Principles

The implementation follows the general project philosophy:

* Joomla Core remains untouched.
* Bootstrap provides only the functional foundation.
* Visual appearance is completely controlled by the template.
* SCSS is the single source of styling.
* JavaScript is only used where necessary.
* Accessibility has priority over visual effects.

---

# 4. Navigation Concept

The template provides a primary navigation consisting of:

* Logo / Branding
* Main Menu
* Optional Search
* Optional CTA Button

Desktop devices display a horizontal navigation bar.

Mobile devices use an offcanvas navigation.

---

# 5. Joomla Integration

The navigation is based entirely on the Joomla menu module.

Recommended module position:

```
menu
```

The menu module is published once and assigned to the desired menu.

The template itself controls only the layout and styling.

---

# 6. Responsive Behaviour

## Desktop

* Horizontal navigation
* Dropdown menus
* Hover support
* Keyboard navigation
* Visible active menu item

---

## Tablet

Depending on available width:

* reduced spacing
* optional earlier switch to mobile menu

---

## Mobile

Navigation is displayed using Bootstrap Offcanvas.

Characteristics:

* Hamburger button
* Slide-in navigation
* Touch friendly
* Automatic closing after menu selection
* Focus trapping
* ESC closes navigation

---

# 7. Bootstrap Components

The following Bootstrap components are used:

| Component | Purpose                    |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| Navbar    | Basic navigation structure |
| Offcanvas | Mobile navigation          |
| Collapse  | Optional fallback          |
| Dropdown  | Submenus                   |
| Container | Layout                     |
| Utilities | Spacing and alignment      |

Bootstrap provides the functionality only.

Visual appearance is implemented exclusively through custom SCSS.

---

# 8. Accessibility

The navigation follows WCAG recommendations.

Requirements:

* Keyboard navigation
* Logical tab order
* Visible focus states
* ARIA labels
* Correct button semantics
* Screen reader compatibility
* Sufficient contrast
* No hover-only interaction

Special attention is given to mobile accessibility.

---

# 9. SCSS Structure

```
scss/
└── components/
    ├── _navigation.scss
    ├── _menu.scss
    ├── _dropdown.scss
    └── _offcanvas.scss
```

Responsibilities:

### _navigation.scss

General navigation layout.

### _menu.scss

Desktop menu styling.

### _dropdown.scss

Dropdown appearance.

### _offcanvas.scss

Mobile navigation.

---

# 10. JavaScript

The template uses Bootstrap's JavaScript components.

Custom JavaScript is only added when Bootstrap functionality is insufficient.

Possible enhancements:

* Scroll detection
* Sticky navigation effects
* Dynamic header shrinking
* Automatic menu closing
* Active section highlighting

---

# 11. Performance

The navigation should:

* minimise DOM complexity
* avoid unnecessary JavaScript
* use CSS transitions instead of JavaScript animations
* avoid layout shifts
* load instantly

---

# 12. SEO Considerations

Navigation contributes significantly to internal linking.

Recommendations:

* Semantic `<nav>` element
* Meaningful menu labels
* Logical hierarchy
* Clean HTML structure
* Crawlable links
* No JavaScript-only navigation

---

# 13. Future Extensions

Possible future enhancements include:

* Mega Menu
* Breadcrumb integration
* Sticky navigation
* Secondary navigation
* Language switcher
* User menu
* Search overlay
* Dark mode switch

These features are intentionally excluded from the initial implementation.

---

# 14. Dependencies

The navigation depends on:

* Joomla 5
* Bootstrap 5
* Joomla Web Asset API
* Template SCSS architecture

No third-party navigation libraries are required.

---

# 15. Architecture Decision

The project deliberately relies on Joomla's native menu system combined with Bootstrap's functional components.

This approach offers several advantages:

* Full Joomla compatibility
* Update safety
* Reduced maintenance effort
* Consistent accessibility support
* Minimal custom JavaScript
* Easy future extensions

Visual design remains completely under the control of the WissensWerk design system and is independent of Bootstrap's default appearance.

